deps/redis/src/config.h and solarisfixes.h are BendKV's: stand-ins for
Redis's, which give sha1.c the byte order and nothing. Three changes to
Lua and its libraries. Every conversion of a number to a C integer
(luaconf.h's lua_number2int and lua_number2integer, and casts in
lstrlib.c, lua_struct.c, lua_cmsgpack.c and lua_cjson.c) goes through
three functions added to luaconf.h, which give the results of Redis's
x86-64 builds (gcc) where C leaves a plain cast undefined. Two fixes
of Redis's, which Ubuntu 24.04's Redis 7.0.15 carries as it applies
them: CVE-2024-31449 (lua_bit.c, Redis's commit 1f7c148) and
CVE-2025-49844 (lparser.c, Redis's commit d5728cb). And luaH_getnum's
test of an integer key against a table's array (ltable.c), which
subtracted 1 from the key, as Redis 7.2's ltable.c writes it: the same
answers, without the overflow that C leaves undefined for the smallest
int.
